753 0 obj
<<
/Title (Centralizes user and access management.  Enhances security through role-based permissions.  Simplifies user administration and monitoring.  Prevents unauthorized access to applications and data. Improves collaboration by assigning appropriate access levels.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 755 0 R
/Next 751 0 R
>>
endobj
754 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Users interface provides a centralized location for managing all users within a Zoho Creator organization. Administrators can add new users, search for existing users, and filter user records)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 752 0 R
/Next 756 0 R
>>
endobj
755 0 obj
<<
/Title (Benefits)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 757 0 R
/Next 753 0 R
>>
endobj
756 0 obj
<<
/Title (based on specific criteria. The interface displays essential information such as the user's Name, Email Address, Assigned Role, and Account Status, making it easier to monitor and manage user access.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 754 0 R
/Next 758 0 R
>>
endobj
757 0 obj
<<
/Title (Add and manage users within the organization.  Assign roles and permission levels using role-based access control. Search and filter users for efficient management.  View user details such as name, email address, role, and account status. Monitor active and inactive user accounts.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 758 0 R
/Next 755 0 R
>>
endobj
758 0 obj
<<
/Title (Zoho Creator uses role-based access control \(RBAC\) to ensure that each user has the appropriate level of access based on their responsibilities. For example, a Super Admin has complete administrative privileges, while other users can be assigned roles with limited permissions. This approach enhances security by ensuring users can access only the applications and features relevant to their roles.  Key Functions)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 756 0 R
/Next 757 0 R
>>
endobj
